WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.850
Donald Trump has reportedly suggested firing
impeachment inquiry witnesses who are working

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.050
at the white house effectively what would
end their tenure at the white house and send

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.330
them back to where they came from, so to speak.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:18.590
Typically other departments, so as an example,
Lieutenant Colonel Alexander Veneman who testified

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.590
yesterday.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:23.460
The way that this works is that different
employees from different departments are sort

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.090
of loaned to the white house for specific
jobs, and many of the people who have been

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:33.399
testifying over the last week, bill Taylor
for example, they're still working for the

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:38.679
government and sometimes for the Trump administration
in some way, even if not in the position they

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:45.089
held at the time of the Ukraine phone call,
which their testimony now focuses on.

00:00:45.089 --> 00:00:49.809
On the one hand, Donald Trump has been talking
about let's fire these people.

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:55.059
On the other hand, he doesn't actually seem
to know that some continue to work for him

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:56.569
in some capacity.

00:00:56.569 --> 00:01:01.781
And it's truly one of these, uh, uh, comedies
of errors that seem so common in the Trump

00:01:01.781 --> 00:01:02.869
administration.

00:01:02.869 --> 00:01:07.710
Trump lashed out yesterday, for example at
witness Jennifer Williams Williams works for

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.630
his vice president Mike Pence, saying she
should read the transcripts, very strange

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:18.390
attacks on someone that, uh, works for the
government and was employed directly by your

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.610
vice president.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:24.649
And what's really important to understand
is that some of the witnesses appeared voluntarily,

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:27.960
but other witnesses appeared under subpoena
as they said.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:33.049
Can you imagine firing someone for responding
to a subpoena?

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:36.250
In most administrations, it would be unthinkable.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:41.729
In this administration, it seems almost to
be the default position to ignore legal constitutional

00:01:41.729 --> 00:01:42.729
subpoenas.

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:46.719
So maybe they actually think people who respond
to subpoenas as required by the law are doing

00:01:46.719 --> 00:01:51.670
something wrong and they deserve to be fired,
very different standards that are applied

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.069
under the current administration.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:58.009
Um, another example is once again, yesterday's
witness, Lieutenant Colonel Alexander Veneman,

00:01:58.009 --> 00:02:03.020
who confirmed a great portion of the narrative
of bribery and extortion that we've heard

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.020
so far.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.220
Veneman is on the national security council
sort of on loan from the defense department.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.670
The idea that's been floated is to fire Veneman
from the NSC, but what about firing him from

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:20.000
the defense department if he's truly what
the Trumpists are portraying him to be, which

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.430
is a dual loyal, which we'll get to, not credible,
whatever.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.159
Why should he even be allowed to stay at the
defense department?

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:31.319
It doesn't make sense because none of this
makes sense.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:35.400
Then his lawyer made it clear that Veneman
is on the national security council until

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.600
next summer.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.319
Whether he will be allowed to stay, we don't
know.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:42.450
Now a reasonable person would say, why would
they do this?

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.959
This makes them look more guilty.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:49.900
This, this could count as witness intimidation
for future witnesses who consider appearing.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.580
Why would they do this?

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.019
This is how Trump operates.

00:02:53.019 --> 00:02:58.760
He doesn't realize or doesn't care that these
obstructive actions call more attention to

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.409
what he might've done.

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:05.151
Your mistake in questioning this strategy
is believing that there is a strategy, there

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.380
is no strategy.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:12.470
These are just Trump's reactions, Trump's
behavior and his reflexive reactions and choices

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.060
make a lot more sense.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.620
If you think of him not as a president but
more like a mob boss, then his choices become

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.230
far more clear and of course we'll see what
happens.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.939
We'll see what repercussions there are for
the people who are participating in the impeachment

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:32.010
hearings, legal, impeachment hearings, individuals
who are showing up, including putting themselves

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:37.829
and their families at risk as we will talk
about soon, the idea that they are the problem

00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:43.810
when they're exposing the problem is sickening,
but unfortunately it goes beyond just job

00:03:43.810 --> 00:04:11.230
threats and that's what we need

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:28.600
to

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:43.750
talk

00:04:43.750 --> 00:05:30.470
about next.

